1
00:00:02,214 --> 00:00:07,350
The Life Of Muhammad ﷺ, Madinan Period Volume 2

2
00:00:07,792 --> 00:00:09,728
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:11,074 --> 00:00:14,316
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:17,611
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد

5
00:00:17,786 --> 00:00:20,405
وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

6
00:00:20,429 --> 00:00:22,282
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمةُ الله وَبَرَكَاتُه

7
00:00:22,417 --> 00:00:29,354
Another Sariyyah(سرية) and the important part of it is the story of Muhallim Bin Jassama(محلم بن جثامة).

8
00:00:29,741 --> 00:00:34,205
Muhallim Bin Jassama(محلم بن جثامة) was a Muslim in this Sariyyah(سرية).

9
00:00:34,803 --> 00:00:43,918
They were traveling and a man called Aamir Bin Azbat al-Ashjaee(عامر بن عضبط ألأشجعي) pass them by

10
00:00:44,164 --> 00:00:46,640
 and when he pass by he said, Assalam O Alaikum(السلام عليكم)!

11
00:00:47,307 --> 00:00:49,652
This is the greeting of Muslims.

12
00:00:50,141 --> 00:00:54,339
Muhallim Bin Jassama(محلم بن جثامة) rushes out and kills this man.

13
00:00:54,984 --> 00:00:59,152
This man who just gave them Salaam(سلام), he went and killed him

14
00:00:59,456 --> 00:01:03,951
because he knew him from the time of Jahilliyah(جاهلية) and there was a problem between them,

15
00:01:04,336 --> 00:01:09,923
so he sought revenge, even though the man said, Assalam O Alaikum(السلام عليكم).

16
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:16,635
So, the chief of the tribe of the murdered came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, Oyeyna Bin Badr(عيينه بن بدر).

17
00:01:16,675 --> 00:01:21,339
 And he's asking for the blood for retribution.

18
00:01:21,910 --> 00:01:27,775
And the chief of the tribe of Muhallim(محلم), also came to Rasool Ullah, Al-Aqra'a Bin Habis(اَلْأقْرَاع بن حابس)

19
00:01:27,847 --> 00:01:30,223
asking Rasool Allah ﷺ leniency.

20
00:01:30,716 --> 00:01:35,605
Rasool Allah ﷺ wants to prevent Fitnah(فِتْنَه) from occurring between these two tribes,

21
00:01:35,930 --> 00:01:39,596
and because it's a feudal society, the Society of Arabia.

22
00:01:39,620 --> 00:01:43,581
So Rasool Allah ﷺ wants(to prevent Fitnah), because in the situation like this, it's Qatl Amd(قتل عمد).

23
00:01:44,258 --> 00:01:45,551
There are two options,

24
00:01:45,598 --> 00:01:50,367
the two options are given to the Oulea(أولياء) of the deceased.

25
00:01:50,407 --> 00:01:51,993
The family members of the deceased

26
00:01:52,159 --> 00:01:59,691
they can choose between asking for the execution of the one who murdered,

27
00:01:59,915 --> 00:02:03,650
 or accepting the blood money which is 100 camels.

28
00:02:03,853 --> 00:02:08,623
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wants to convince them to accept the blood money, in order to prevent the Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

29
00:02:09,439 --> 00:02:10,838
Oyeyna Bin Badr(عيينه بن بدر) said;

30
00:02:10,869 --> 00:02:11,869
لَا وَلله

31
00:02:11,921 --> 00:02:12,973
In the name of Allah.

32
00:02:13,138 --> 00:02:18,189
لَا اَعْدَآئه حَتَّى اُضِيْقَ نِسَائُه’ مِنَّ الْحُزْنِ مِثْلَ مَا اَضَاقَ نِسَائِيْ

33
00:02:18,264 --> 00:02:20,502
In the name of Allah I'm not gonna leave him alone until,

34
00:02:20,542 --> 00:02:25,113
I have his women taste the sorrow that my women have tasted.

35
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,062
He must be killed.

36
00:02:27,322 --> 00:02:34,204
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Take 50 camels from me now and 50 camels, when we return into Madina.

37
00:02:34,535 --> 00:02:36,898
They refused, he offered them a second time.

38
00:02:36,923 --> 00:02:43,090
Rasool Allah ﷺ kept on trying to solve this problem until, eventually they agreed and they accepted the blood money.

39
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:45,555
So, now the people of Muhallim(محلم),

40
00:02:45,844 --> 00:02:48,297
they told Muhallim(محلم) go to Rasool Allah ﷺ

41
00:02:48,351 --> 00:02:52,849
and tell him to ask for your forgiveness, to ask Allah to forgive you,

42
00:02:53,008 --> 00:02:56,728
so Muhallim(محلم) came and he was already dressed in garments prepared for execution.

43
00:02:56,753 --> 00:02:58,545
I mean he was prepared for death.

44
00:02:58,632 --> 00:03:02,831
So, he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he was described as being a tall heavyset man.

45
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:05,123
He came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and sat down and said;

46
00:03:05,163 --> 00:03:09,365
O Messenger of Allah, I am Muhallim(محلم) ask Allah to forgive me.

47
00:03:09,934 --> 00:03:10,828
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

48
00:03:10,868 --> 00:03:12,455
  اَللَّهُمَّ لَا تَغْفِرْلِيْ مُحَلِّم

49
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:14,482
O Allah do not forgive Muhallim(محلم).

50
00:03:14,849 --> 00:03:17,545
He said: O Rasool Ullah, ask Allah to forgive me.

51
00:03:17,817 --> 00:03:18,567
He ﷺ said it again.

52
00:03:18,655 --> 00:03:21,188
 اَللَّهُمَّ لَا تَغْفِرْلِيْ مُحَلِّم

53
00:03:21,516 --> 00:03:23,461
O Allah do not forgive Muhallim(محلم).

54
00:03:23,498 --> 00:03:25,130
The narrator of the Hadith(حديث) says, that

55
00:03:25,154 --> 00:03:28,970
Muhallim(محلم) stood up covering his face to cover his tears.

56
00:03:29,650 --> 00:03:34,091
And this is another lesson in the sanctity of the blood of a Muslim.

57
00:03:35,031 --> 00:03:44,839
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذَا ضَرَبْتُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ فَتَبَيَّنُوا

58
00:03:45,564 --> 00:03:54,244
فَتَبَيَّنُوا وَلَا تَقُولُوا لِمَنْ أَلْقَىٰ إِلَيْكُمُ السَّلَامَ لَسْتَ مُؤْمِنًا

59
00:03:54,941 --> 00:04:02,669
تَبْتَغُونَ عَرَضَ الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا فَعِنْدَ اللَّهِ مَغَانِمُ كَثِيرَةٌ

60
00:04:03,296 --> 00:04:12,080
كَذَٰلِكَ كُنْتُمْ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَمَنَّ اللَّهُ عَلَيْكُمْ فَتَبَيَّنُوا

61
00:04:12,429 --> 00:04:18,900
 إِنَّ اللَّهَ كَانَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرًا۝

62
00:04:19,573 --> 00:04:23,495
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Ayah(آية), O you who have believed

63
00:04:24,236 --> 00:04:28,695
when you go forth to fight in the cause of Allah, investigate

64
00:04:28,993 --> 00:04:32,358
and do not say to one who gives you Salam(سلام)

65
00:04:32,485 --> 00:04:36,926
you are not a believer aspiring for the goods, of worldly life

66
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:40,027
because Muhallim(محلم) he took over the camel of this man,

67
00:04:40,186 --> 00:04:42,786
aspiring for the goods of worldly life.

68
00:04:42,912 --> 00:04:45,792
For with Allah are many acquisitions.

69
00:04:46,446 --> 00:04:48,936
You, yourself were like that before.

70
00:04:48,975 --> 00:04:51,890
Meaning, there was a time when you were disbelievers.

71
00:04:52,044 --> 00:04:55,920
Then Allah conferred his favour upon you, so investigate

72
00:04:56,055 --> 00:04:59,550
indeed Allah is ever with, what you do acquainted.

73
00:05:00,227 --> 00:05:01,677
Then there's another Sariyyah(سرية)

74
00:05:01,701 --> 00:05:05,132
and this is the Sariyyah(سرية) of Abdullah Bin Hudaffa As-Sahmi رضي الله عنه.

75
00:05:05,409 --> 00:05:07,859
Abdullah Bin Hudaffa(عبدالله بن حذافة) one of the Sahabah رضي الله عنه,

76
00:05:07,883 --> 00:05:09,154
he was sent out in a Sariyyah(سرية).

77
00:05:09,607 --> 00:05:12,780
The members of his Sariyyah(سرية) they did something that angered him.

78
00:05:13,348 --> 00:05:18,712
So he was very upset, they had this fire, bonfire.

79
00:05:18,926 --> 00:05:20,609
He told them, jump into it,

80
00:05:21,244 --> 00:05:24,713
he told the members of his Sariyyah(سرية), to jump into the fire.

81
00:05:25,028 --> 00:05:26,629
He said; I am the Ameer(أمير)

82
00:05:27,057 --> 00:05:31,651
and you know that the Ta'ah(طاعة) of the Ameer(أمير) is Wajib(واجب) following the Ameer(أمير) is mandatory,

83
00:05:31,691 --> 00:05:33,186
 so jump into the fire.

84
00:05:33,823 --> 00:05:38,493
They refused, the Sahabah(صحابه) refused, and then he calm down after that

85
00:05:38,518 --> 00:05:43,144
and when they returned to Rasool Allah ﷺ and they asked him about the situation

86
00:05:43,168 --> 00:05:44,979
what did Rasool Allah ﷺ say?. He said;

87
00:05:45,003 --> 00:05:49,956
لَوْ دَخَلُوْهَا مَا خَرَجُوْا مِنْهَا اِنَّمَا الطَّاعَةْ فِيْ الْمَعْرُوْفَ

88
00:05:50,091 --> 00:05:57,064
If they entered into that fire, they would never have left it because obedience is in good.

89
00:05:57,379 --> 00:06:02,538
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying, that if they jumped into that fire, they would have remained in Hellfire

90
00:06:02,973 --> 00:06:08,150
because you should only obey the Ameer(أمير) when he instructs you to do good

91
00:06:08,203 --> 00:06:10,692
but he if he orders you to do evil

92
00:06:10,896 --> 00:06:14,184
then you do not follow him. And this Hadith(حديث) is Muttafiq Alaih(متفق عليه),

93
00:06:14,351 --> 00:06:15,536
 so the rule is,

94
00:06:15,576 --> 00:06:18,577
لَا طَاعَة لْمَخْلُوْقِ فِيْ مَعْصِيَة الْخَالِقْ

95
00:06:18,676 --> 00:06:23,646
We should not obey the creation, in disobeying the Creator.

96
00:06:24,144 --> 00:06:29,190
As long as the Ameer(أمير) gives instructions that are Halal(حلال) and allowed then we follow.

97
00:06:29,327 --> 00:06:33,152
As soon as they tell us to do something that is Haram(حرام) we refuse.

98
00:06:33,972 --> 00:06:38,346
So, if the ruler orders that the women should take out their Hijab(حجاب)

99
00:06:38,497 --> 00:06:40,996
then that order should be disobeyed

100
00:06:41,147 --> 00:06:47,966
if the ruler orders Muslims to not fast in Ramadan(رمضان) because it affects productivity

101
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:49,335
then we must disobey

102
00:06:49,642 --> 00:06:53,167
if the ruler bans Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

103
00:06:53,191 --> 00:06:54,608
than he should be disobeyed.

104
00:06:54,698 --> 00:06:59,364
If the ruler wants the Muslims to be loyal to the Yahood(يهود) and the Christians

105
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:03,595
and to be disloyal towards the ones who are practicing the religion of Allah

106
00:07:03,732 --> 00:07:05,017
he should be disobeyed

107
00:07:05,576 --> 00:07:09,020
so the ruler is obeyed, when he instructs good

108
00:07:09,093 --> 00:07:12,316
and he is disobeyed, when he's instructing evil.

109
00:07:12,857 --> 00:07:13,857
Umra Tul Qadhaa(عُمرة الْقَضاء),

110
00:07:14,095 --> 00:07:20,355
Rasool Allah ﷺ, the time has arrived to go and make Umrah(عمرة)

111
00:07:20,764 --> 00:07:26,038
one year has passed since the signing of the treaty of Hudaybiyya(حديبية).

112
00:07:26,544 --> 00:07:31,819
So, the Muslims, who were with him in Hudaybiyya(حديبية), joined him now to make Umrah(عمرة).

113
00:07:32,848 --> 00:07:36,234
Rasool Allah ﷺ, the agreement that he had with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), is that

114
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:42,460
 he would only carry with him, the weapons of the traveler swords in their sheaths

115
00:07:42,746 --> 00:07:48,172
but Rasool Allah ﷺ brought with him other weapons bows, arrows, spears

116
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:51,058
and when they reached close to Makkah.

117
00:07:51,336 --> 00:08:01,179
The news was carried, that Rasool Allah ﷺ has brought arms other than the swords, so he must be preparing for war.

118
00:08:01,682 --> 00:08:04,738
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) said: We have done nothing wrong.

119
00:08:05,050 --> 00:08:09,999
We did not break any of the agreements or the terms of the conditions of the agreement.

120
00:08:10,208 --> 00:08:13,503
Why is Muhammadﷺ attacking us?

121
00:08:14,451 --> 00:08:18,794
So, some of them went to Muhammadﷺ, and they told him;

122
00:08:18,834 --> 00:08:22,781
يَا مُحَمَّدْمَا عُرِفْتَ صَغِيْرًا وَلَا كَبِيْرًابِالْغَدْرْ

123
00:08:23,227 --> 00:08:29,577
تَدْخُلُ بِّالسلَاحِ عَلَى قَوْمِكَ فِيْ الْحَرَمْ وَقَدْ شَرَطَّت لَهُمْ اَن لَّا تَدْخُلَ اِلَّا بِسلَاحٍ مُسَافِرَ سُيُوْفِ قَرَّبْ

124
00:08:29,625 --> 00:08:36,022
O Muhammad(محمد), you were not known, when you were young, or when you were old to betray,

125
00:08:36,358 --> 00:08:41,405
you want to enter with weapons into Haram(حرم), against your people.

126
00:08:41,590 --> 00:08:43,574
And you have given them the condition that

127
00:08:43,598 --> 00:08:47,118
you will only enter with the weapons of the traveler, swords in their sheaths

128
00:08:47,142 --> 00:08:48,126
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

129
00:08:48,166 --> 00:08:49,829
اِنِّيْ لَا اَدْخُلُهَا بِالسلَاحٍ

130
00:08:50,326 --> 00:08:52,973
I will not enter with these weapons.

131
00:08:53,436 --> 00:08:54,335
Mickraz(مِكْرَزْ) said:

132
00:08:54,503 --> 00:08:57,463
هَذَ الَّذِيْ تُعْرَفْ بِهْ، اَلْبِرُّ وَالْوَفَاءْ

133
00:08:57,605 --> 00:09:04,053
This is what you are known to be a man of your word Birr(بِر) and Wafa'a(وفا) is good

134
00:09:04,201 --> 00:09:08,470
and honesty and Wafa'a(وفا) is keeping one's word

135
00:09:08,569 --> 00:09:13,587
So, over here, you can notice that, this was the reputation of Muhammadﷺ

136
00:09:13,981 --> 00:09:17,857
and this is the Shahadah(شهادة) the witness of the Kuffar(كفار)

137
00:09:18,069 --> 00:09:21,779
that he is a man of truth, and a man of his word.

138
00:09:22,224 --> 00:09:26,874
And this is an important thing brothers and sisters to practice.

139
00:09:27,501 --> 00:09:33,301
 There's a Muslim character there are Muslim morals, there's a Muslim standard of conduct,

140
00:09:33,721 --> 00:09:39,041
we should uphold these virtues in our dealings with Muslim and non Muslim

141
00:09:39,772 --> 00:09:44,200
because we do it for the sake of Allah, and it is Ibadah(عبادة).

142
00:09:44,734 --> 00:09:49,473
This is what the Kuffar(كفار) knew about Muhammadﷺ, that he was a man of truth

143
00:09:50,024 --> 00:09:54,569
As-Sadiq(الصادق), Al-Ameen(ألأمين) the trustworthy and the truthful.

144
00:09:55,154 --> 00:10:01,360
And in peace and war, the conduct of Rasool Allah ﷺ was the same

145
00:10:01,694 --> 00:10:07,991
his character was that of a Muslim, the virtues of Islam, he was the living Qur'an(قرآن).

146
00:10:08,504 --> 00:10:15,583
And it's important for us to live up to the standard of morals in Islam.

147
00:10:16,064 --> 00:10:21,860
Rasool Allah ﷺ brought these weapons with him because he needed it as a protection, as a safeguard

148
00:10:22,050 --> 00:10:24,800
 but he was going to leave them outside of Makkah

149
00:10:25,108 --> 00:10:28,012
and enter into Makkah only with his swords.

150
00:10:29,031 --> 00:10:30,333
They entered into Makkah

151
00:10:30,373 --> 00:10:35,893
and the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) they had, this hatred and this jealousy and animosity in their hearts,

152
00:10:35,933 --> 00:10:42,756
they couldn't even stand being around the Muslims, so they vacated Makkah for three days

153
00:10:42,796 --> 00:10:48,334
 to allow Muhammadﷺ and the Muslims in there and they don't want to be with them

154
00:10:48,610 --> 00:10:51,588
but they were on top of the mountains surrounding Makkah

155
00:10:51,628 --> 00:10:55,067
and they were looking at the Muslims.

156
00:10:55,522 --> 00:10:59,502
And they were saying among themselves that now the Muslims are going to come

157
00:10:59,765 --> 00:11:05,555
and they are going to be weak, feeble because of the fever of Madina.

158
00:11:05,587 --> 00:11:13,675
You remember we talked about the Madina was famous of this is endemic diseases that existed in there.

159
00:11:14,099 --> 00:11:16,936
So the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were saying that,

160
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:20,898
يَدْخُلْ عَلَيْنَا مُحَمَّدْ وَالْمُسْلِمُوْنْ وَ قَدْ وَهَنَتْهُمْ حمى يَثْرِبْ

161
00:11:21,483 --> 00:11:24,026
The fever of Madina has made them weak.

162
00:11:24,568 --> 00:11:28,364
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ cared about the reputation of Muslims

163
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:30,738
and he wanted to give an image of strength

164
00:11:31,652 --> 00:11:33,494
so he told the Muslims;

165
00:11:34,078 --> 00:11:37,248
to uncover their right shoulder

166
00:11:37,668 --> 00:11:43,629
and not to walk around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) as was the custom

167
00:11:44,109 --> 00:11:46,131
but to do what is called the Ramel(رَمَلْ).

168
00:11:46,274 --> 00:11:52,058
 Ramel(رَمَلْ) is walking fast with strength it's like marching.

169
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,250
So, the Muslims would do that.

170
00:11:55,217 --> 00:11:58,531
But between Rukn-e-Yamani(ركن أليماني) and Hijr-e-Aswad(حجر ألأسود)

171
00:11:58,571 --> 00:12:01,800
because they would be concealed from the kuffar(كفار), the Kuffar(كفار) cannot see them

172
00:12:01,824 --> 00:12:03,649
they would walk normally.

173
00:12:03,751 --> 00:12:07,082
So, now brothers and sisters, if you go to Umrah(عمرة) or Al-Hajj(حَجْ),

174
00:12:07,106 --> 00:12:09,864
you would notice that the Sunnah(سنة) is that

175
00:12:10,553 --> 00:12:16,718
in the first three rounds, you would walk very fast, in this what's called the Ramel(رَمَلْ) it's like marching

176
00:12:17,059 --> 00:12:21,765
 but between Hijr-e-Aswad(حجر ألأسود) and Rukn-e-Yamani(ركن أليماني) you would walk normally.

177
00:12:21,805 --> 00:12:22,400
Why?

178
00:12:22,531 --> 00:12:27,754
because that was the area where the Ka'aba(كعبه) was covered the Muslims from the eyes of the Kuffar(كفار).

179
00:12:27,978 --> 00:12:30,902
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want to exhaust the Muslims.

180
00:12:31,092 --> 00:12:31,955
But in the same time,

181
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:35,264
he didn't want the Kuffar(كفار) to take the impression that the Muslims are weak

182
00:12:35,501 --> 00:12:40,886
so he had them do this Ramel(رَمَلْ), around three corners or three sides of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

183
00:12:41,167 --> 00:12:42,966
while the forth side they would walk

184
00:12:43,223 --> 00:12:46,152
and if it wasn't for the fact that it was truly exhaust the Muslims

185
00:12:46,192 --> 00:12:49,992
he would have, had them do it for the seven rounds.

186
00:12:50,771 --> 00:12:53,658
Even though this was done with that objective

187
00:12:53,824 --> 00:12:56,976
but the Sunnah(سنة) remained and we still do it, until this day.

188
00:12:57,438 --> 00:13:04,159
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent one of the Sahabah(صحابه) to do the engagement

189
00:13:04,183 --> 00:13:07,588
he wanted to get married to Maimoonah Bint Al-Haris(ميمونه بنت ألحارث).

190
00:13:08,362 --> 00:13:15,367
Maimoonah(ميمونة), she agreed, and she said: My Wali(ولي), to sign the contract would be Al-Abbas(العباس).

191
00:13:15,776 --> 00:13:18,394
Al-Abbas(العباس) was married to her sister Umm Ul-Fazal(أم الفضل)

192
00:13:19,070 --> 00:13:22,937
and Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to hold the Walimah(وليمه) in Makkah

193
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:25,700
but the three days were over.

194
00:13:25,986 --> 00:13:29,818
So Huwaitib Ibn Abdul Uzza(حويطب إبن عبدالعزى) he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

195
00:13:30,207 --> 00:13:33,072
اُنَاشِدَكَ الله وَالْعهدَ الَذِيْ بَيْنَنَا

196
00:13:33,507 --> 00:13:37,747
I ask you in the name of Allah and the contract between us to leave.

197
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:42,149
I mean, they have this hatred to Rasool Allah ﷺ and they couldn't stand the Muslims

198
00:13:42,189 --> 00:13:44,397
 and they were waiting for the three days to finish

199
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:47,627
and they immediately, came asking the Muslims to leave.

200
00:13:47,667 --> 00:13:49,098
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them;

201
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:51,716
I have married a woman from among you

202
00:13:51,985 --> 00:13:54,904
it won't harm you if I finished my wedding to her

203
00:13:55,146 --> 00:13:57,741
and we prepare a feast and you can join us.

204
00:13:57,876 --> 00:14:02,050
You're welcome to come, and join this Walima(وليمه).

205
00:14:02,158 --> 00:14:04,608
They said: We ask you in the name of Allah to leave.

206
00:14:04,798 --> 00:14:09,275
Now, when they came to him, Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting with some of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار)

207
00:14:09,299 --> 00:14:11,551
Saad Ibn Ubadah(سعدابن عبادة) and other Ansaar(أنْصَار).

208
00:14:12,284 --> 00:14:15,717
And they said; We want you to leave from our land.

209
00:14:16,058 --> 00:14:18,826
So, Saad Ibn Ubadah(سعدابن عبادة) angrily responded back and said;

210
00:14:18,850 --> 00:14:21,258
This is not your land or the land of your fathers.

211
00:14:21,992 --> 00:14:27,029
Rasool Allah ﷺ calmed him down and said: We would leave, and they left.

212
00:14:27,377 --> 00:14:33,457
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ held whatever remained from the celebration of his wedding,

213
00:14:33,646 --> 00:14:36,862
he held it outside of Makkah in a place called Sarf(سرف)

214
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,875
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله),

215
00:14:39,097 --> 00:14:45,936
 Maimoonah(ميمونة) later on would end up dying in the same place where she married Rasool Allah ﷺ.

216
00:14:46,725 --> 00:14:51,972
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was leaving from Makkah, the daughter of Hamza(حمزه), young girl

217
00:14:52,329 --> 00:14:55,237
she came running saying Ya Amm(يا عَمّْ), Ya Amm(يا عَمّْ), Ya Amm(يا عَمّْ), Ya Amm(يا عَمّْ).

218
00:14:55,261 --> 00:14:57,113
O Uncle, O Uncle, O Uncle.

219
00:14:57,967 --> 00:14:59,783
So, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) grabbed her

220
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:09,828
and handed her over to Fatima(فاطمه) and said take care of your cousin, to take her back to Madina

221
00:15:10,348 --> 00:15:12,548
Jafar(جعفر) said: No, I'm going to take her.

222
00:15:12,996 --> 00:15:16,152
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said: I am her cousin,

223
00:15:16,532 --> 00:15:19,261
Jafar(جعفر) said: I'm her cousin too,

224
00:15:19,592 --> 00:15:25,936
and then Zaid(زيد) came in and said; She is the daughter of my uncle.

225
00:15:26,530 --> 00:15:31,273
So, what happened was Rasool Allah ﷺ came in, to judge between them.

226
00:15:31,297 --> 00:15:36,445
Because of this conflict the voices were..... Ya'ani(يعني) they had a conflict among them

227
00:15:36,469 --> 00:15:41,784
who will take care of the daughter of Hamza رضي الله عنه.

228
00:15:42,223 --> 00:15:48,332
So, Rasool Ullah came to judge between them and he handed her over to Jafar(جعفر)

229
00:15:48,675 --> 00:15:53,222
because Jafar(جعفر) was married to her Aunt, to the Aunt of the daughter of Hamza(حمزه).

230
00:15:53,484 --> 00:15:58,458
Zaid(زيد) Actually he said: She's the daughter of my uncle

231
00:15:58,482 --> 00:16:03,635
because Zaid(زيد) was the adopted son of Muhammadﷺ and

232
00:16:03,887 --> 00:16:06,001
Hamza(حمزه) is the Uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ

233
00:16:06,041 --> 00:16:11,418
but also Hamza(حمزه) is the brother of Rasool Allah ﷺ because of breastfeeding.

234
00:16:11,923 --> 00:16:16,412
The same woman breastfed, both Muhammadﷺ and Hamza(حمزه)

235
00:16:16,437 --> 00:16:20,248
so Hamza(حمزه) is the uncle of Rasool Ullah and his brother in Radha'a(رضَاعى) too.

236
00:16:20,985 --> 00:16:26,000
So, that makes the daughter of Hamza(حمزه) the Cousin of Zaid(زيد),

237
00:16:26,452 --> 00:16:31,269
Rasool Allah ﷺ handed her over to Jafar(جعفر) and then Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ali(علي)

238
00:16:31,662 --> 00:16:33,545
اَنْتَ مِنِّيْ وَ اَنَا مِنْكْ

239
00:16:33,878 --> 00:16:36,888
You are from me, and I am from you.

240
00:16:37,356 --> 00:16:40,456
And he told Jafar Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه

241
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:42,883
اَشْبَهْتَ خَلْقِيْ وَخُلُقِيْ

242
00:16:43,391 --> 00:16:46,731
You are our similar to me in manners and in looks,

243
00:16:47,442 --> 00:16:50,718
and he told Zaid Ibn Harissa رضي الله عنه.

244
00:16:50,748 --> 00:16:52,563
اَنْتَ اَخُوْنَا وَ مَوْلَانَا

245
00:16:52,899 --> 00:16:55,650
You are our brother and our companion.

246
00:16:55,988 --> 00:17:00,214
And then Ali Bin Abi Talib رضي الله عنه he told Rasool Allah ﷺ

247
00:17:00,239 --> 00:17:02,906
wouldn't you marry Hamza(حمزه)'s daughter.

248
00:17:03,401 --> 00:17:08,297
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: She is the daughter of my brother from breastfeeding, Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري),

249
00:17:08,337 --> 00:17:13,262
which makes her Mahrum(محرم) for him, he cannot therefore marry her.

250
00:17:13,638 --> 00:17:18,422
We are done with the events of the seventh year of Hijrah(هجرة).

251
00:17:18,807 --> 00:17:24,308
Now, we move on to the events of the eighth year of Hijrah(هجرة) and this is a very busy year.

252
00:17:24,589 --> 00:17:29,729
We have the Islam of Khalid(خالد), Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) and Uthman Ibn Talha(عُثمان ابن طلحه)

253
00:17:30,182 --> 00:17:32,734
 then we have the battle of Mao'ta(مؤته).

254
00:17:33,412 --> 00:17:37,650
The first proper battle between the Muslims and Roman Empire,

255
00:17:37,992 --> 00:17:42,933
and then there's Fattah Makkah(فتح مكه) and the great battle of Hunain(حنين)

256
00:17:43,091 --> 00:17:44,749
and the siege of At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف).

257
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:46,487
So, it's a very busy year.

258
00:17:46,879 --> 00:17:50,271
We'll start with the story of the Islam of Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) and Khalid(خالد).

259
00:17:50,359 --> 00:17:57,268
Amr Bin Aas رضي الله عنه said: I fought against Rasool Allah ﷺ in the Battle of Badr(بدر)

260
00:17:57,292 --> 00:17:58,379
and Allah saved me.

261
00:17:58,782 --> 00:18:02,267
And then I fought against Muhammadﷺ in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد)

262
00:18:02,417 --> 00:18:03,430
and Allah saved me,

263
00:18:03,847 --> 00:18:07,119
then I fought against Muhammadﷺ in the Battle of Khandaq(خندق)

264
00:18:07,261 --> 00:18:08,269
and Allah saved me.

265
00:18:08,363 --> 00:18:11,054
Now when is Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) speaking, saying this.

266
00:18:11,078 --> 00:18:12,776
He's saying this after I became Muslim.

267
00:18:12,883 --> 00:18:15,252
So, now he's looking back at his memories.

268
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:20,484
And he's thinking about him and saying, Man, I was, I was fighting the Messenger of Allah,

269
00:18:20,801 --> 00:18:22,748
what in the world was I doing?

270
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:27,185
I mean, then being a Mushrik(مشرك), being a disbeliever,

271
00:18:27,831 --> 00:18:29,844
the way he would think about things is different.

272
00:18:29,869 --> 00:18:32,381
And now when he looks back at it, and say wait a minute,

273
00:18:32,406 --> 00:18:34,832
I was fighting against the Messenger of Allah.

274
00:18:35,291 --> 00:18:37,172
And these are the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم,

275
00:18:37,196 --> 00:18:39,920
who loved Rasool Allah ﷺ, more than anything in the world.

276
00:18:40,037 --> 00:18:45,245
So, after every battle, he would say, and Allah saved me, meaning if I died then,

277
00:18:45,616 --> 00:18:47,052
I would have been in hellfire.

278
00:18:47,767 --> 00:18:51,336
So, he's going through his history. He said;

279
00:18:51,667 --> 00:18:55,185
I fought against Rasool Allah ﷺ in Badr(بدر), and then I fought against him in Uhud(أحَد)

280
00:18:55,213 --> 00:18:57,230
and then I fought against him in Al-Khandaq(الخندق)

281
00:18:58,049 --> 00:19:04,070
and I was beginning to feel that, no matter what Muhammad(محمد) is gonna win!

282
00:19:04,739 --> 00:19:12,995
His armies are getting better and better, his Da'wah(دعوة) is spreading more and more

283
00:19:13,328 --> 00:19:19,293
and we are getting more constricted and narrowed in our movement day after day.

284
00:19:19,870 --> 00:19:25,507
So, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) was starting to feel this conflict and depression

285
00:19:26,011 --> 00:19:29,386
that a Kafir(كافر) would have when he sees the victory of Islam.

286
00:19:29,414 --> 00:19:36,241
I mean there's so much built up envy, jealousy, hatred that builds up in the hearts of the Kuffar(كفار).

287
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:38,103
I mean, you have to keep in mind that

288
00:19:38,127 --> 00:19:41,440
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) is the one who's dominating the heart of the disbeliever,

289
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:46,700
so all of these feelings are bottled up inside the heart of Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص)

290
00:19:47,089 --> 00:19:50,909
so he just had enough of it and he decided that he's going to leave Makkah

291
00:19:51,187 --> 00:19:53,629
and go and stay in a place called Al-Wahat(ألْوَحَتْ) .

292
00:19:53,995 --> 00:19:57,626
he took his family, he took his wealth and he went there and he said;

293
00:19:57,698 --> 00:19:59,176
وَاَقْلَلْتُ مِنَّ النَّاسْ

294
00:19:59,513 --> 00:20:01,200
And I stayed away from people.

295
00:20:02,388 --> 00:20:04,071
He just want to stay away from everyone,

296
00:20:04,221 --> 00:20:08,614
and then, when the contract of Al-Hudaybiyya(ألْحُدَيْبِيه) occurred,

297
00:20:09,132 --> 00:20:14,681
when Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were forced to admit the existence of the Islamic State

298
00:20:14,845 --> 00:20:19,603
and they were forced to admit the authority of Muhammadﷺ.

299
00:20:19,992 --> 00:20:23,190
I mean when some of the Sahabah(صحابه) complained about Uhud(أحَد),

300
00:20:23,859 --> 00:20:29,975
Rasool Allah ﷺ reminded them about the days of Uhud(أحَد), the early days of Islam and he told them;

301
00:20:30,182 --> 00:20:33,534
 Now Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have accepted peace from you.

302
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:38,120
He was turning their attention to the great developments that were occurring

303
00:20:39,286 --> 00:20:42,167
and we said that Hudaybiyya(ألْحُدَيْبِيه) was a great victory for Islam.

304
00:20:42,191 --> 00:20:46,928
So, Al-Hudaybiyya(ألْحُدَيْبِيه) when it happened, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص),

305
00:20:47,532 --> 00:20:51,982
he said tomorrow Muhammad(محمد) will enter into Makkah, it's inevitable.

306
00:20:52,740 --> 00:20:54,505
Muhammadﷺ is going to come in,

307
00:20:54,900 --> 00:21:03,056
it reached to the degree that Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have been unable to fight him, when he's at the doorsteps of Makkah,

308
00:21:03,626 --> 00:21:05,662
and they accepted to sign a treaty with him,

309
00:21:06,185 --> 00:21:12,614
this is a sign of the fact that sooner or later Muhammadﷺ will enter into Makkah.

310
00:21:13,701 --> 00:21:17,103
So, he ruled out staying in Makkah, and he ruled out staying in At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف)

311
00:21:17,221 --> 00:21:21,159
and these are the two major cities of Al-Hijaaz(ألحجاز),

312
00:21:21,659 --> 00:21:25,672
he called some of the members of his clan.

313
00:21:25,751 --> 00:21:29,965
 And Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) was a man who was respected among his people

314
00:21:30,340 --> 00:21:34,136
and they used to listen to him, and they see to him as being their guide.

315
00:21:34,685 --> 00:21:39,641
So, he called these people who had trust in him, and he told them;

316
00:21:40,142 --> 00:21:46,708
اِنِّيْ اَرى اَمْرَ محمد يَعُّلُو الْاُمُوْرَا كُلَّهَا، عُلُّوًا مُنْكَرَا

317
00:21:47,359 --> 00:21:55,768
I can see that the affair of Muhammad(محمد) is rising above all others in a horrible way.

318
00:21:56,402 --> 00:22:01,052
I mean, he's seeing the events unfolding in front of his eyes.

319
00:22:01,077 --> 00:22:05,990
And through his wisdom and intelligence, he can read through these events in history

320
00:22:06,030 --> 00:22:15,295
 and see that Muhammadﷺ and Islam are slowly but surely rising, and rising, and rising against everything else.

321
00:22:15,694 --> 00:22:17,132
I can see this with my own eyes.

322
00:22:17,172 --> 00:22:22,935
And he's a disbeliever, but he can sense and feel that, he can see it,

323
00:22:23,581 --> 00:22:26,076
just like some of the Kuffar(كفار) today can see it.

324
00:22:26,301 --> 00:22:29,524
While unfortunately many of the Muslims are failing to see it

325
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:33,320
and they are deep in their sleep, and they cannot see

326
00:22:33,598 --> 00:22:38,283
what is happening and unfolding of the events, the Ummah(امة) today,

327
00:22:38,741 --> 00:22:43,205
and they are failing to see the victory of Allahعَزّوجَلّ  that is on its way.

328
00:22:43,933 --> 00:22:46,493
So, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), told his people;

329
00:22:46,910 --> 00:22:51,797
Therefore, I don't think it's a good idea for us to stay in Makkah.

330
00:22:52,576 --> 00:22:58,178
Rather, I believe that we should go and stay with An-Najashi(النجاشي), in Abyssinia.

331
00:22:58,617 --> 00:23:01,418
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) had a good relationship with An-Najjashi(ألنجاشي).

332
00:23:01,977 --> 00:23:05,695
So, he wanted to put that into use and he said, let's go and stay over there.

333
00:23:06,146 --> 00:23:14,208
If Muhammadﷺ is victorious, then we are away from him.

334
00:23:14,790 --> 00:23:17,781
And if he loses and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) wins

335
00:23:18,211 --> 00:23:21,758
then Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they already know who we are, and what our position is.

336
00:23:22,317 --> 00:23:24,276
And Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said about himself,

337
00:23:24,723 --> 00:23:28,435
and I would see that if all Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) became Muslim, I would never become Muslim.

338
00:23:28,460 --> 00:23:32,188
I mean, that's how much hatred he had in his heart to Islam.

339
00:23:32,347 --> 00:23:37,538
If all of my people, every single one of them in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) becomes Muslim, I'm not.

340
00:23:39,025 --> 00:23:41,905
So, they agreed with his assessment and opinion

341
00:23:42,111 --> 00:23:47,811
and they decided to travel together and go to Abyssinia, to leave their land, to make Hijrah(هجرة).

342
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:52,524
What is the driving force behind that, it is Hatred towards Islam.

343
00:23:53,547 --> 00:23:56,986
He said; Let's take gifts for An-Najashi(النجاشي),

344
00:23:57,010 --> 00:24:00,883
and the thing that An-Najashi(النجاشي) loved most was Hide, leather.

345
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:06,215
So, his people gathered all what they could from the best hide they could find.

346
00:24:06,541 --> 00:24:11,251
And they took a boat and went to An-Najashi(النجاشي), in Abyssinia.

347
00:24:12,210 --> 00:24:14,923
They went to visit An-Najashi(النجاشي).

348
00:24:15,717 --> 00:24:22,185
And who did they find coming out from the court of An-Najashi(النجاشي), Amr Bin Umayyah Ad-Dhamri(عمرو بن أمَيَّة اَلضَمْرِي),

349
00:24:22,423 --> 00:24:30,725
 who was sent by Rasool Allah ﷺ to perform the marriage of Rasool Allah ﷺ to the daughter of Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان), Umm Habiba(ام حبيبه)

350
00:24:31,196 --> 00:24:37,065
and also to call the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) of Abyssinia to go back to Madina.

351
00:24:37,636 --> 00:24:44,739
So, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), saw him coming out from the court of An-Najashi(النجاشي), the Palace of An-Najashi(النجاشي).

352
00:24:45,571 --> 00:24:52,236
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) entered, obviously he entered alone, the rest of his companions had to wait for him.

353
00:24:52,979 --> 00:24:58,256
And he went and made Sajood(سجود) to the king, as was the tradition

354
00:24:58,723 --> 00:25:00,884
and he was very well received.

355
00:25:01,144 --> 00:25:02,192
An-Najashi(النجاشي) told them;

356
00:25:02,232 --> 00:25:06,041
 Welcome my friend, have you brought me any gifts from your land.

357
00:25:06,231 --> 00:25:07,541
He said: Yes, I did.

358
00:25:07,962 --> 00:25:10,530
King O King, I have brought you some Hide.

359
00:25:11,347 --> 00:25:16,965
And then he presented the king with the pieces of Hide that he has brought

360
00:25:17,179 --> 00:25:19,850
the king was very happy and pleased with it.

361
00:25:20,024 --> 00:25:24,955
And right then and there he distributed some of it to his patriarchs,

362
00:25:25,297 --> 00:25:29,916
and then the rest he ordered that it would be registered and recorded,

363
00:25:30,182 --> 00:25:33,208
and then deposited and kept in a safe place.

364
00:25:33,858 --> 00:25:36,670
And then Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), he got carried away

365
00:25:37,123 --> 00:25:40,757
he saw how well the reception was, and how happy the king was with the gift.

366
00:25:41,100 --> 00:25:47,033
So, he told the king: O King, I have seen a man come out from your palace

367
00:25:47,927 --> 00:25:53,593
who is the Messenger of our enemy, the man who has killed the noble among us,

368
00:25:54,439 --> 00:25:59,392
would you hand him over to me, so that we could kill him.

369
00:26:00,204 --> 00:26:05,949
An-Najashi(النجاشي) immediately hit Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) in the face

370
00:26:06,223 --> 00:26:10,245
and Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: I thought that my nose was broken,

371
00:26:10,395 --> 00:26:16,371
and blood started flowing out of my nostrils, and I was covering it with my clothes,

372
00:26:16,572 --> 00:26:19,930
and I wish that the Earth would swallow me

373
00:26:20,392 --> 00:26:24,551
because of the embarrassment I felt and the fear I felt from the king.

374
00:26:25,744 --> 00:26:27,236
And then Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said;

375
00:26:27,482 --> 00:26:34,459
If I knew, O King if I knew that you dislike what I said, I wouldn't have said it.

376
00:26:35,965 --> 00:26:38,260
And then the king said, An-Najashi(النجاشي) said;

377
00:26:38,284 --> 00:26:40,510
يَا عمْرو تَسْألُنِيْ

378
00:26:40,698 --> 00:26:43,936
You are asking me O Amr(عمرو), to hand you over

379
00:26:44,269 --> 00:26:48,175
the Messenger of the man who receives An-Namoos Al-Akbar(أناموس ألأكبر),

380
00:26:48,199 --> 00:26:50,192
and An-Namoos Al-Akbar(ألناموس ألأكبر) is Jibreel عليه السّلام.

381
00:26:50,523 --> 00:26:52,634
O Amr(عمرو) you're asking me,

382
00:26:53,063 --> 00:26:58,210
to hand over to you the messenger of the man who receives An-Namoos Al-Akbar(ألناموس ألأكبر),

383
00:26:58,234 --> 00:26:59,589
so that you may kill him.

384
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:06,006
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: Right then and there I had a change of heart,

385
00:27:06,420 --> 00:27:12,724
and I told myself: The Arabs and the non Arabs recognize the truth and I do not.

386
00:27:13,577 --> 00:27:15,940
And that is when my heart changed.

387
00:27:15,965 --> 00:27:16,504
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله),

388
00:27:16,543 --> 00:27:19,606
look at how Allahسُبْحَانه وتعالى guided Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

389
00:27:19,654 --> 00:27:22,822
He lived with Rasool Allah ﷺ Thirteen(13) years in Makkah

390
00:27:22,900 --> 00:27:27,636
and he knew him, very well and he did not become Muslim then

391
00:27:27,693 --> 00:27:33,793
 and he becomes a Muslim in the court of An-Najashi(النجاشي) in a foreign land,

392
00:27:33,982 --> 00:27:38,102
in that particular moment, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said I told An-Najashi(النجاشي).

393
00:27:38,246 --> 00:27:40,131
اَتَشْهَدْ بِذَالِكْ

394
00:27:40,474 --> 00:27:42,865
Is that you witnesses, is that your testimony?

395
00:27:43,613 --> 00:27:44,472
An-Najashi(النجاشي) said;

396
00:27:44,503 --> 00:27:46,932
نَعَمْ اَشْهَدُ عِنْدَاللهِ بِهْ

397
00:27:47,410 --> 00:27:50,845
I testify with that in front of Allah

398
00:27:51,349 --> 00:27:52,010
and then he said;

399
00:27:52,133 --> 00:27:54,690
يَا عمْرو، اَطَّعْنِيْ وَاتببِعْ

400
00:27:55,077 --> 00:27:57,128
فَوَلله اِنَّهْ لَعَلَى الْحَقْ

401
00:27:57,392 --> 00:28:01,983
وَلَيَظْهَرَنَّ عَلَى مَنْ خَالَفَه’ كَمَا ظَهَرَ مُوْسَى عَلَى فِرْعَوْنَ وَجُنُوْدِهْ

402
00:28:02,296 --> 00:28:05,045
O Amr(عمرو), listen to me and follow him

403
00:28:05,166 --> 00:28:11,254
because in the name of Allah, he is on truth and he will prevail against all of his enemies.

404
00:28:11,349 --> 00:28:14,661
Just like Musa(موسى) prevailed against Firoun(فرعون) and his soldiers.

405
00:28:16,079 --> 00:28:21,827
An-Najashi(النجاشي) in this faraway land, this is his testimony about Rasool Allah ﷺ.

406
00:28:21,882 --> 00:28:25,792
An-Najashi(النجاشي) was a man of truth, he was a man who understood religion,

407
00:28:25,999 --> 00:28:27,757
he was a man who understood history,

408
00:28:27,781 --> 00:28:30,677
he was a man who understood the lives of the prophets,

409
00:28:31,434 --> 00:28:35,314
and he is giving Da'wah(دعوة) to Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

410
00:28:35,537 --> 00:28:37,702
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) who knows Rasool Allah ﷺ,

411
00:28:37,726 --> 00:28:42,662
knows about Islam and knows about the Muslims is receiving Da'wah(دعوة) from An-Najashi(النجاشي).

412
00:28:43,789 --> 00:28:47,152
You know the way Da'wah(دعوة) works, it defies all logic,

413
00:28:48,046 --> 00:28:53,616
therefore we should not have any fixed beliefs about it,

414
00:28:53,948 --> 00:28:57,103
and you can see throughout the Da'wah(دعوة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, amazing things,

415
00:28:57,144 --> 00:28:59,526
Abu Talib(ابوطالب) does not become Muslim,

416
00:28:59,788 --> 00:29:02,795
while you have Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari(أبوذرألغفاري) becoming Muslim.

417
00:29:03,557 --> 00:29:06,496
Abu Lahab(أبولهب) the uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ does not become Muslim

418
00:29:06,520 --> 00:29:09,799
and Salman Al-Farisi(سلمان ألفارسي) comes all the way from Persia and becomes Muslim,

419
00:29:10,301 --> 00:29:11,750
it defies all rules.

420
00:29:11,955 --> 00:29:14,773
Hidaya(هدايه), guidance is something that belongs to Allah.

421
00:29:14,814 --> 00:29:17,489
إِنَّكَ لَا تَهْدِي مَنْ أَحْبَبْتَ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشَاءُ ۚ

422
00:29:17,605 --> 00:29:21,571
You do not guide those whom you want, it is Allah, Who guides whom He wills.

423
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:28,232
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: At that moment, I gave him baiyah(بيعة) to become Muslim.

424
00:29:28,894 --> 00:29:33,598
And An-Najashi(النجاشي) took my pledge to follow and Obey Rasool Allah ﷺ and become Muslim.

425
00:29:34,956 --> 00:29:39,686
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) came with an intention and is coming back with another intention,

426
00:29:39,734 --> 00:29:44,442
 he came for an objective and now he's coming a completely different human being.

427
00:29:44,822 --> 00:29:45,351
 Subhan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)

428
00:29:45,383 --> 00:29:47,754
 وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُودَ رَبِّكَ إِلَّا هُوَ ۚ

429
00:29:47,778 --> 00:29:50,298
Nobody knows about the soldiers of Allah but He.

430
00:29:50,629 --> 00:29:52,371
An-Najashi(النجاشي) was a soldier of Allah

431
00:29:52,394 --> 00:29:55,807
and through him, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) this great man(becomes Muslim)

432
00:29:55,940 --> 00:30:01,331
and you can read the history of Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) and see what Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) did for Islam.

433
00:30:01,975 --> 00:30:06,981
His Da'wah(دعوة), his acceptance of Islam came through An-Najashi(النجاشي)

434
00:30:07,993 --> 00:30:12,821
and he was such a great enemy of a Islam and now he becomes a Muslim.

435
00:30:13,419 --> 00:30:17,770
An-Najashi(النجاشي) then ordered some new clothes to be brought for me

436
00:30:17,863 --> 00:30:19,670
because of my clothes were soaked in blood.

437
00:30:20,002 --> 00:30:23,955
And then I came out and when my companion saw me wearing some new clothes,

438
00:30:24,006 --> 00:30:26,631
 they were quite happy, and they felt that things were going well.

439
00:30:26,741 --> 00:30:28,439
Before I went in I told them,

440
00:30:28,479 --> 00:30:32,762
that I'm going to try to convince An-Najashi(النجاشي) to hand me over Amr Bin Umayyah Ad-Dhamri(عمرو بن أمَيَّة اَلضَمْرِي),

441
00:30:32,802 --> 00:30:34,146
so that I could kill him.

442
00:30:34,233 --> 00:30:38,432
And this would gain a good reputation for us with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

443
00:30:38,834 --> 00:30:40,223
So, now they asked him, What did he do?

444
00:30:40,247 --> 00:30:45,723
He said, Well, I didn't feel that was good to propose this to him in our first meeting, but I will do that next time.

445
00:30:45,763 --> 00:30:47,132
They said: That's a good idea.

446
00:30:47,768 --> 00:30:52,944
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: I said I'm going to go for some business I have

447
00:30:53,550 --> 00:30:56,648
and he didn't tell him what his plans were, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) left.

448
00:30:56,722 --> 00:31:01,703
He took a boat and went towards Madina, he just left them without a word.

449
00:31:01,871 --> 00:31:07,876
These men who, he brought out with intention of fleeing away from Muhammadﷺ.

450
00:31:07,987 --> 00:31:12,884
As soon as he reaches, he leaves them in Abyssinia and goes to Muhammadﷺ.

451
00:31:13,989 --> 00:31:15,624
You know, Hidaya(هدايه) is a strange thing.

452
00:31:16,222 --> 00:31:19,236
So, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) reached to a place called Sha'aibah(شُعَيْبَه)

453
00:31:19,276 --> 00:31:22,317
and then he goes and reaches Marr Az-Zahraan(مَرَّ ألظَهْرَان),

454
00:31:22,540 --> 00:31:25,810
when he gets to this place called Marr Az-Zahraan(مَرَّ ألظَهْرَان)

455
00:31:25,978 --> 00:31:28,998
and he's traveling towards the Madina, he sees two men,

456
00:31:29,022 --> 00:31:32,942
one of them was in a tent and the other one was tying the camels.

457
00:31:33,188 --> 00:31:34,400
Who were these two men?

458
00:31:34,511 --> 00:31:37,470
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and Uthman Ibn Talha(عثمان إبن طلحه),

459
00:31:37,618 --> 00:31:39,134
he walked up to them and said;

460
00:31:39,677 --> 00:31:40,673
What are you doing?

461
00:31:41,341 --> 00:31:42,327
Where are you going?

462
00:31:42,768 --> 00:31:48,650
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said: There's no one left, no one worthy left

463
00:31:49,061 --> 00:31:55,840
and Muhammadﷺ, he is prevailing, so we want to go and become Muslim.

464
00:31:55,864 --> 00:31:58,382
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: This is the same reason that brought me

465
00:31:58,406 --> 00:32:01,930
and I see this also at the striking thing

466
00:32:02,384 --> 00:32:10,545
that, these men who were, say among the leaders of the effort to fight the Islam Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

467
00:32:10,973 --> 00:32:17,420
and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) he belongs to the family of Bannu Makhzoom(بنو مخزوم) who were enemies of Islam,

468
00:32:17,469 --> 00:32:20,949
his father many Ayaat(آيات) were revealed about his father

469
00:32:21,273 --> 00:32:24,369
and then also Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) belongs to the same family

470
00:32:24,887 --> 00:32:26,867
and then you have Uthman Ibn Talha(عثمان إبن طلحه).

471
00:32:26,891 --> 00:32:29,697
Uthman Ibn Talha(عثمان إبن طلحه) belongs to Bannu Abd-Ad-Daar(بنوعبد ألدار)

472
00:32:29,872 --> 00:32:34,671
very noble family in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they were the ones, who carry the banner in war,

473
00:32:34,696 --> 00:32:36,714
and they're the ones who hold the key of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

474
00:32:36,739 --> 00:32:38,728
and by the way, they still hold, until this day,

475
00:32:38,926 --> 00:32:44,597
the key is inherited from father to son all the way until this day.

476
00:32:44,806 --> 00:32:49,435
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said: The key should remain among you until the Day of Judgment,

477
00:32:49,559 --> 00:32:52,480
no one shall take it from you but a transgressor.

478
00:32:52,813 --> 00:32:57,443
So, these three men belong to these prominent families in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

479
00:32:57,862 --> 00:32:59,410
and they're very important figures

480
00:32:59,663 --> 00:33:01,113
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)

481
00:33:01,392 --> 00:33:03,318
they all meet together, I mean what a coincidence

482
00:33:03,358 --> 00:33:08,416
and nothing is a coincidence, everything happens through the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, it's preordained.

483
00:33:08,693 --> 00:33:12,816
Now, we're talking about 20 years fighting Islam

484
00:33:13,163 --> 00:33:18,046
and they meet along the path to Madina,

485
00:33:18,134 --> 00:33:21,478
so that they would travel and enter Madina together, the three of them.

486
00:33:22,232 --> 00:33:25,247
They reach to the outskirts of Madina

487
00:33:25,696 --> 00:33:27,432
and they hear somebody say;

488
00:33:27,472 --> 00:33:29,488
يا رباح ،يا رباح، يا رباح

489
00:33:29,524 --> 00:33:35,212
Rabbah(رباح) the derivative of Rabbah(رباح) is Ribh(رِبْحْ) and that means profit,

490
00:33:35,677 --> 00:33:36,942
something that you gain.

491
00:33:37,135 --> 00:33:39,866
So, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: We took it as a good omen,

492
00:33:40,353 --> 00:33:42,438
and then someone saw us and said;

493
00:33:42,463 --> 00:33:45,992
قَدْ اَلْقتْ مَكَّهْ اِلَيْكُمْ مَقَالِيْدَ هَا بَعْدَهَذَيْنْ

494
00:33:46,197 --> 00:33:50,819
Makkah has handed over its reins to you after these two men

495
00:33:51,021 --> 00:33:53,643
and he was referring to Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

496
00:33:53,694 --> 00:34:01,405
meaning that who is left in Makkah, after Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) become Muslim.

497
00:34:01,490 --> 00:34:07,931
It is as if Makkah has handed over its reins to Rasool Allah ﷺ after these men became Muslim.

498
00:34:08,401 --> 00:34:10,767
Because as I said, you know

499
00:34:10,954 --> 00:34:17,089
these men they constitute the second generation of leadership that was fighting Islam,

500
00:34:17,136 --> 00:34:24,833
 I mean you have the first generation and these are Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), Abu Lahab(ابولهب), Umayyah Bin Khalaf(أمَيَّة بن خلف),

501
00:34:25,005 --> 00:34:28,868
Ubaye Bin Khalaf(أبَي بن خلف), Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان), Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(ألْوَلِيد بن مُغِيرَة)

502
00:34:29,030 --> 00:34:34,832
these were the prominent personalities, who're leading the effort to fight Islam,

503
00:34:34,977 --> 00:34:37,877
in the early days up to the Battle of Badr(بدر).

504
00:34:37,991 --> 00:34:42,131
The Battle of Badr(بدر) was the day in which the forces of evil were crushed

505
00:34:42,300 --> 00:34:47,553
and the entire first generation of leadership was exterminated,

506
00:34:48,206 --> 00:34:51,589
the only one that remained from those men was Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان).

507
00:34:52,320 --> 00:34:53,893
He is the only man who survived

508
00:34:53,917 --> 00:34:57,037
and the reason he survived is because he didn't attend Badr(بدر).

509
00:34:57,701 --> 00:35:01,609
Because the whole reason why Badr(بدر) occurred was to protect his caravan that he was leading.

510
00:35:02,497 --> 00:35:06,823
Utba Bin Rabiyah(عُتْبَة بن ربيعة), Shaybah(شَيْبَة), Al-Waleed(وَليد), Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل),

511
00:35:06,847 --> 00:35:10,034
Umayyah Bin Khalaf(أمَيَّة بن خلف), Ubaye Bin Khalaf(أبَي بن خلف), they were all killed.

512
00:35:10,343 --> 00:35:12,870
And some of them already died before that like a Abu Lahab(ابولهب).

513
00:35:13,281 --> 00:35:16,749
And I mean, he didn't die in the Battle of Badr(بدر), he died in Makkah.

514
00:35:17,402 --> 00:35:21,116
So the next generation that took over leadership

515
00:35:21,550 --> 00:35:25,341
where people like Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), Ikrimah Bin Abi Jahal(عكْرِمَة بن أبي جهل)

516
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:28,553
and Sufwaan Ibn Umayyah(صَفْوَان ابن أمَيَّة), Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

517
00:35:29,096 --> 00:35:32,598
So they represented the new blood, the new leadership in Makkah,

518
00:35:32,720 --> 00:35:40,626
for these men to become Muslim was such a devastating blow, to the people of Makkah

519
00:35:40,810 --> 00:35:44,812
and that's why this man saw it as if Makkah has lost it, and that's it,

520
00:35:44,867 --> 00:35:51,637
they're handing over the reins of leadership to Rasool Allah ﷺ, after the Islam of these men.

521
00:35:52,273 --> 00:35:56,330
They came into Madina and Rasool Allah ﷺ was eagerly waiting for them

522
00:35:56,772 --> 00:35:59,897
smiling all the time while they're walking towards him,

523
00:35:59,921 --> 00:36:05,298
they can see this beaming smile on the face of Rasool Allah ﷺ, he was so happy for their Islam

524
00:36:05,518 --> 00:36:06,755
and this is the true Da'wah(دعوة),

525
00:36:06,795 --> 00:36:13,256
and Rasool Allah ﷺ didn't have anything against them even though they are fought against him in Battlefield,

526
00:36:13,296 --> 00:36:19,431
 they've spoken against him, they have harmed him, they have driven him out of his land

527
00:36:19,544 --> 00:36:23,858
but Rasool Allah ﷺ was looking at the interest of Islam.

528
00:36:24,253 --> 00:36:28,707
And was happy because these men are now going to become soldiers of Allah.

529
00:36:29,726 --> 00:36:30,740
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said;

530
00:36:30,764 --> 00:36:34,869
I told Rasool Allah ﷺ, O Rasool Ullah I pledge my allegiance to you

531
00:36:35,239 --> 00:36:39,682
with the condition that Allah forgives for me all my past sins.

532
00:36:39,731 --> 00:36:45,004
He said: I forgot to ask Him to forgive them for me, my forthcoming sins.

533
00:36:45,217 --> 00:36:46,881
Rasool Allah ﷺ told me;

534
00:36:47,088 --> 00:36:51,010
يَا عمْرو، اَمَا تَعْلَمْ اَنَّ الْاِسْلَامَ يَجُّبُ مَا قَبْلَهَا

535
00:36:51,082 --> 00:36:53,846
وَاَنَّ الْهِجْرَۃ تَجُبُّ مَا قَبْلَهَا

536
00:36:53,947 --> 00:36:56,195
وَ اَنَّ الْحَجَّ يَجُبُّ مَا قَبْلَهَا

537
00:36:56,371 --> 00:36:59,894
O Amr(عمرو), don't you know that Islam erases everything before it,

538
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:03,064
and that Hijrah(هجرة) erases everything before it

539
00:37:03,170 --> 00:37:05,775
and that Hajj(حَجْ) erases everything before it.

540
00:37:05,822 --> 00:37:07,841
So, these 3 deeds, they erase everything.

541
00:37:08,229 --> 00:37:11,113
So, you can see how important Hajj(حَجْ) and Hijrah(هجرة) are,

542
00:37:11,176 --> 00:37:15,824
Rasool Allah ﷺ equated them to Islam, that they erase everything that occurs before.

543
00:37:16,508 --> 00:37:21,415
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said; Rasool Allah ﷺ took a lot of care of us

544
00:37:21,771 --> 00:37:26,379
and he used to put us ahead of many of the companions

545
00:37:26,633 --> 00:37:29,966
and that remained to be the case until he passed away.

546
00:37:30,157 --> 00:37:36,267
And then the same thing with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he took a lot of care of me and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

547
00:37:36,392 --> 00:37:39,183
and then in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

548
00:37:39,215 --> 00:37:45,398
he used to give a lot of attention to me and appoint me in important positions of responsibility.

549
00:37:45,423 --> 00:37:48,692
However, the relationship between Umar(عُمَر) and Khalid(خالد) as he says,

550
00:37:48,717 --> 00:37:50,319
كَانَ كَالْعَاتِبْ عَلَى خَالِد

551
00:37:50,753 --> 00:37:54,532
He was disapproving of some of the actions of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

552
00:37:54,802 --> 00:37:57,882
So, this is the story accordingly to the narration of Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

553
00:37:57,963 --> 00:38:01,465
We'll see what Khalid Ibn Waleed رضي الله عنه said, Khalid(خالد) said;

554
00:38:01,853 --> 00:38:10,192
 قَدْ شَهِدْ تَّ هَذِهِ الْمَوَاطِنْ كُلَّهَا عَلَى محمدٍ صلى الله عليه وسلم فَلَيْسَ فِيْ مَوْطِنْ اَشْهَدُه’ اِلَّا اَنْصَرِفْ

555
00:38:10,230 --> 00:38:15,744
وَاَنَا اَرَى فِيْ نَفْسِيْ اَنِّيْ مُوْضِعٌ فِيْ غَيْرِ شَيْء وَ اَنَّ مُحمَّدً سَيَظْهَرْ

556
00:38:16,305 --> 00:38:23,311
He said: I have attended all of these battles against Muhammad(محمد),

557
00:38:23,940 --> 00:38:30,943
and in every situation I attend, I leave with this feeling in my heart

558
00:38:30,967 --> 00:38:34,783
that I'm putting my effort in something that is wasted

559
00:38:35,093 --> 00:38:37,478
and that in the end, Muhammad(محمد) will prevail.

560
00:38:37,739 --> 00:38:40,959
So, we had this deep feeling in his heart that what he's doing is wrong,

561
00:38:41,023 --> 00:38:44,916
there is something wrong with it, and that this man will be victorious and will prevail

562
00:38:45,763 --> 00:38:48,609
he said until, Hudaybiyya(ألحديبية) came,

563
00:38:49,114 --> 00:38:53,142
he said; I lead a contingent of Kuffar(كفار) two hundred men

564
00:38:53,381 --> 00:38:57,428
and Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Muslims were praying Salaat-uz-Zohar(صلاة الظهر),

565
00:38:57,467 --> 00:39:03,491
he said: I was face to face I met Muhammadﷺ face to face while they were praying

566
00:39:03,735 --> 00:39:07,271
and that was my opportunity to attack them in Salah(صلاة).

567
00:39:07,588 --> 00:39:10,160
But I was reluctant to do so.

568
00:39:10,421 --> 00:39:14,312
Now, this word coming from Khalid Ibn Waleed رضي الله عنه is strange

569
00:39:14,336 --> 00:39:18,355
because he was the furthest from being a reluctant person

570
00:39:18,379 --> 00:39:20,743
he was a very decisive man.

571
00:39:20,832 --> 00:39:26,134
So, for Khalid(خالد) to say that I was reluctant to attack him, and he said, and that was good,

572
00:39:26,279 --> 00:39:27,583
Allah saved him

573
00:39:27,736 --> 00:39:29,502
and he was reluctant at that moment

574
00:39:29,526 --> 00:39:34,676
because Allahعَزّوجَلّ wanted something good for Khalid Ibn Waleed رضي الله عنه.

575
00:39:35,532 --> 00:39:39,029
He said: So Salah(صلاة) finished I didn't take that opportunity,

576
00:39:39,422 --> 00:39:42,348
so I decided that I'm going to attack them, in Salaat-Ul-Asr(صلاة العصر)

577
00:39:42,372 --> 00:39:44,517
he said: By the time they came to pray Asr(عصر),

578
00:39:44,541 --> 00:39:47,131
Rasool Allah ﷺ was already praying Salaat-Ul-Khaof(صلاةالخوف).

579
00:39:47,155 --> 00:39:51,774
Salah(صلاة) where half of the army prays and half of them protects the rest.

580
00:39:51,997 --> 00:39:54,227
فَعَلِمْتُ اَنَّ الرَّجُلَ مَمْنُوْعَ

581
00:39:54,282 --> 00:39:56,343
I knew that this man is being protected.

582
00:39:57,418 --> 00:40:00,952
So, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) carries on with the narration and says;

583
00:40:00,978 --> 00:40:05,912
When Rasool Allah ﷺ came the following year to do Umra-Tul-Qadhaa(عُمْرَةُالْقَضَاء),

584
00:40:06,219 --> 00:40:08,459
when Rasool Allah ﷺ came to do Umra-Tul-Qadhaa(عُمْرَةُالْقَضَاء),

585
00:40:08,909 --> 00:40:12,052
his brother, Al-Waleed Bin Waleed(ألوليد بن وليد) came looking for him.

586
00:40:12,424 --> 00:40:18,257
Now, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was among the Kuffar(كفار) who vacated Makkah for the Muslims

587
00:40:18,297 --> 00:40:20,412
 because they didn't want to see them, they just left.

588
00:40:20,604 --> 00:40:24,348
So, Al-Waleed(ألوليد) came looking for his brother, Khalid(خالد),

589
00:40:24,569 --> 00:40:27,363
and when he didn't find him, he left him a letter.

590
00:40:27,409 --> 00:40:28,522
What did he say? He said;

591
00:40:28,563 --> 00:40:30,075
بِسْمِ الله الرَحْمن الرَّحِيْمْ۝

592
00:40:30,309 --> 00:40:31,067
اَمَّا بَعْدْ

593
00:40:31,355 --> 00:40:33,523
فَاِنِّيْ لَمْ اَرَى اَعْجَبْ

594
00:40:33,698 --> 00:40:35,537
مِنْ ذَهَابَ رَاْيِكَ عَنِ الْاِسْلَامْ

595
00:40:36,005 --> 00:40:37,429
وَعَقْلُكْ وَعَقْلُكْ

596
00:40:37,855 --> 00:40:40,489
وَ مِثْلُ الْاِسْلَامِ ما جَهلَه’ اَحَدْ؟

597
00:40:40,664 --> 00:40:44,932
وَقَدْ سَاَلَنِيْ رَسُول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم عَنْكَ، وَقَالَ: اَيْنَ خَالِدْ؟

598
00:40:45,184 --> 00:40:46,605
 فَقُلتَ: يَاْتِيْ بِهِ الله

599
00:40:46,913 --> 00:40:49,749
. فَقَالَ: " مَا مِثْلُه’ جَهِلَ الْاِسْلَامْ

600
00:40:49,870 --> 00:40:55,337
وَلَوْ كَانَ جَعَلَ نِكَايَتَه’ وَحْدَه’ مَعَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ كَانَ خَيْرَا لَّهْ

601
00:40:55,506 --> 00:41:01,377
 وَلَقَدَّمْنَاه’ عَلَى غَيْرِهْ"، فَا سْتَدْرِكْ يَا اَخِيْ مَا فَاتَكْ، فَقَدْ فَاتَكَ مَوَاطِنْ صَالِحة

602
00:41:02,181 --> 00:41:02,585
He said;

603
00:41:02,633 --> 00:41:03,919
بِسْمِ الله الرَحْمن الرَّحِيْمْ۝

604
00:41:04,304 --> 00:41:06,974
In the name of Allah the Most Merciful and Most compassionate.

605
00:41:07,338 --> 00:41:12,480
I know of nothing more strange then your antipathy for Islam

606
00:41:12,742 --> 00:41:15,071
being as intelligent as you are.

607
00:41:15,442 --> 00:41:18,592
Could anyone disregard something like Islam.?

608
00:41:18,964 --> 00:41:23,157
Rasool Allah ﷺ has asked me about you, he said; Where is Khalid(خالد),

609
00:41:23,451 --> 00:41:25,201
I replied, Allah will bring him.

610
00:41:25,580 --> 00:41:29,413
He then asked; Could someone like him disregard Islam.

611
00:41:29,933 --> 00:41:35,745
If he were to put his energy and bravery to work with the Muslims, it would be better for him.

612
00:41:35,944 --> 00:41:39,619
We would certainly give him precedents before others.

613
00:41:40,130 --> 00:41:44,279
Take note brother of what good things you are missing.

614
00:41:44,964 --> 00:41:48,307
Rasool Allah ﷺ is asking about Khalid(خالد), where is Khalid(خالد)?

615
00:41:48,939 --> 00:41:52,873
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ is sending Khalid(خالد) a message through his brother.

616
00:41:53,611 --> 00:41:58,317
He's telling him that it's not appropriate for someone like you

617
00:41:58,774 --> 00:42:02,488
as intelligent as you are, to stay away from Islam

618
00:42:03,030 --> 00:42:06,102
and if you become Muslim we'll put you ahead of many others.

619
00:42:06,707 --> 00:42:09,870
This is true Da'wah(دعوة), dear brothers and sisters.

620
00:42:10,796 --> 00:42:15,080
The fact that Rasool Allah ﷺ was asking about him, cares about him

621
00:42:15,236 --> 00:42:16,649
because Khalid(خالد) said;

622
00:42:16,850 --> 00:42:23,032
The question of Rasool Allah ﷺ, when Rasool Allah ﷺ asked about me, that affected me a lot.

623
00:42:23,112 --> 00:42:27,755
 And this is what made Khalid(خالد) decide, to make his move and become Muslim.

624
00:42:28,238 --> 00:42:31,684
It is the fact that Rasool Allah ﷺ had him on his mind

625
00:42:31,708 --> 00:42:35,125
it is the fact that Rasool Allah ﷺ thought about him, gave him a thought,

626
00:42:35,704 --> 00:42:39,510
and to admit that even though he's a Kafir(كافر).

627
00:42:39,543 --> 00:42:45,466
But to say that he's an intelligent man, how could his mind not understand and recognize Islam

628
00:42:46,402 --> 00:42:50,679
and then also the fact, that Rasool Allah ﷺ said: We'll put him ahead of many others.

629
00:42:51,261 --> 00:42:56,208
The status in Islam is according to how early you become Muslim.

630
00:42:56,462 --> 00:42:59,336
I mean, that was the status that the Sahabah(صحابه) held

631
00:42:59,864 --> 00:43:06,093
you have the, the earlier Sahabi(صحابي) becomes Muslim, the higher he is held,

632
00:43:06,777 --> 00:43:15,089
and that is only reasonable because As-sabq(ألسبق) being ahead, shows a state of heart with the person

633
00:43:15,586 --> 00:43:18,772
but here Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying even though Khalid(خالد) may become Muslim late,

634
00:43:18,804 --> 00:43:20,682
but we will put them ahead of many others. Why?

635
00:43:20,886 --> 00:43:24,862
Because of the consideration that Rasool Allah ﷺ had for the status of Khalid(خالد),

636
00:43:25,124 --> 00:43:26,885
his intelligence, his abilities

637
00:43:27,170 --> 00:43:29,491
and this is an important thing for the leader and the Daaiyaah(داعية),

638
00:43:29,597 --> 00:43:32,953
to recognize the abilities of people, people are not the same, they are different.

639
00:43:33,754 --> 00:43:36,081
Some people have qualities that others don't possess

640
00:43:36,105 --> 00:43:38,955
some people have specialties that others don't possess,

641
00:43:38,979 --> 00:43:42,504
some people are strong, some people are weak, some people are intelligent,

642
00:43:42,529 --> 00:43:46,034
some people are less intelligent, you know people are different.

643
00:43:46,058 --> 00:43:49,094
Allah سبحانه وتعالى has divided this Rizq(رزق) among people

644
00:43:49,294 --> 00:43:52,866
and everybody has a different capability

645
00:43:53,081 --> 00:43:58,479
and leadership is the ability to put the right person in the right place.

646
00:43:59,308 --> 00:44:03,859
Khalid Bin Waleed رضي الله عنه decided that he's going to leave and he's going to become Muslim.

647
00:44:04,166 --> 00:44:11,617
And he had a dream he saw himself in a very narrow constricted place

648
00:44:12,363 --> 00:44:17,957
and that's he's walking out of this place into a very vast and beautiful area.

649
00:44:18,211 --> 00:44:20,918
When he asked for the interpretation of the dream later on,

650
00:44:21,038 --> 00:44:25,729
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) told him; It means that, this is you leaving Shirk(شرك) and entering into Islam.

651
00:44:26,544 --> 00:44:27,969
He went to Safwaan(صفوان),

652
00:44:28,129 --> 00:44:31,929
so he wanted to talk to his close friends, Safwaan Ibn Umayyah(صفوان ابن أمية) being one of them.

653
00:44:32,113 --> 00:44:37,726
He went to Safwaan(صفوان) and told him that I want to become Muslim you like to join me.?

654
00:44:37,947 --> 00:44:43,537
Safwaan(صفوان) said; If no one but me remains I'm not gonna become Muslim.

655
00:44:44,298 --> 00:44:50,689
So, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said: Well this is the man whose father and brother were killed by the Muslims.

656
00:44:51,682 --> 00:44:55,451
So, then he went to Ikrimah Bin Abi Jahal(عكرمة بن أبي جهل) he told him;

657
00:44:55,721 --> 00:45:02,196
That our situation is, with the Muslims, with Muhammad(محمد) is like a fox in a hole.

658
00:45:02,349 --> 00:45:05,629
You drop bucket of water over him and he's going to come out running.

659
00:45:06,024 --> 00:45:08,882
In other words, Muhammadﷺ is surrounding us

660
00:45:08,907 --> 00:45:14,680
and we are like fox in a hole and all what Muhammadﷺ and the Muslims have to do is to thou us with a bucket of water,

661
00:45:14,827 --> 00:45:17,659
and we're going to come out running. We have nothing left.

662
00:45:17,876 --> 00:45:21,268
So, what do you think about becoming Muslim. Ikrimah(عكرمة), refused,

663
00:45:21,596 --> 00:45:24,195
so Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) told him well, don't tell anybody about it.

664
00:45:24,495 --> 00:45:29,042
And then Khalid(خالد), he met Uthman Bin Talha(عثمان ابن طلحه), and said how about I talked to him?

665
00:45:29,187 --> 00:45:34,700
And then he said: No, I'm not gonna talk to him because he lost his family in Uhud(أحَد).

666
00:45:34,750 --> 00:45:41,361
I mean, seven family members of Uthman Bin Talha(عثمان ابن طلحه) were killed under the banner of the Mushrikeen(مشركين).

667
00:45:41,661 --> 00:45:43,015
So, he said: I'm not going to speak to him.

668
00:45:43,055 --> 00:45:46,777
And then he said, Well, what difference that it's make, I'm leaving anyway.

669
00:45:46,817 --> 00:45:48,069
So, let me just talk to him.

670
00:45:48,502 --> 00:45:51,550
And he went to Uthman(عثمان) and proposed the idea to him, and

671
00:45:51,574 --> 00:45:55,416
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) he found him to be very receptive and he agreed to go immediately.

672
00:45:56,112 --> 00:46:01,479
And this tells us that we shouldn't have pre judgments about people

673
00:46:01,709 --> 00:46:04,263
and again, we go back to the issue of Hidayah(هداية)

674
00:46:04,511 --> 00:46:11,445
we don't know, who's going to be guided and who won't and we should not rule out anything,

675
00:46:11,469 --> 00:46:14,698
and you should never close the gates of hope for anyone

676
00:46:15,164 --> 00:46:20,455
and this is a man who Khalid(خالد) thought in the beginning that he won't be receptive

677
00:46:20,495 --> 00:46:23,946
and then Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) he found him to be the most receptive among the three.

678
00:46:24,201 --> 00:46:31,327
Even though, he is the one who lost seven of his family members in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

679
00:46:32,083 --> 00:46:37,137
So, never give up on anyone we spread out the message, our responsibility is to give Balaagh(بلاغ)

680
00:46:37,366 --> 00:46:40,891
and then it is Allah(الله), who guides, we're not responsible for the results.

681
00:46:40,915 --> 00:46:44,286
We have to do our part we do it as an Ibadah(عبادة) for Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

682
00:46:44,392 --> 00:46:46,884
But it is Allah who controls the hearts of men.

683
00:46:47,466 --> 00:46:51,527
Khalid(خالد) told Uthman(عثمان), we meet in this particular place

684
00:46:51,791 --> 00:46:54,253
if you arrive before me you wait, until I come,

685
00:46:54,277 --> 00:46:57,559
if I arrived there before you I wait for you, until you come.

686
00:46:58,180 --> 00:47:01,537
They travelled and then they met with Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص)

687
00:47:01,561 --> 00:47:04,706
we already talked about that and when they reached to the outskirts of Madina,

688
00:47:04,851 --> 00:47:09,336
Khalid(خالد) said: We stopped and then we changed our clothes and we put our best clothes on.

689
00:47:09,572 --> 00:47:11,878
This is how they wanted to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ.

690
00:47:11,918 --> 00:47:17,010
They were dressed up in their best clothes to go and meet Rasool Allah ﷺ,

691
00:47:17,226 --> 00:47:20,988
preparing themselves for this, for the greatest moment, in their lives.

692
00:47:21,797 --> 00:47:24,511
And when Khalid(خالد) met Rasool Allah ﷺ,

693
00:47:24,551 --> 00:47:28,192
Rasool Ullah told him come here after he gave his pledge,

694
00:47:28,319 --> 00:47:30,070
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

695
00:47:30,134 --> 00:47:32,630
اَلْحَمدُلله، اَلَّذِيْ هَدَاكْ

696
00:47:33,063 --> 00:47:39,140
 قَدْ كُنْتُ اَرَى لَكَ  عَقْلًا رَجَوْت اَنْ لَّا يُسْلِمَكَ اِلَّا اِلَى خَيْرْ

697
00:47:40,128 --> 00:47:42,911
Al-Hamdolillah(ألْحمدلله), Praise be to Allah, who guided you.

698
00:47:43,580 --> 00:47:46,123
I used to see that you are intelligent

699
00:47:46,502 --> 00:47:52,165
and I hope that your intelligence would only bring you, or only guide you towards good.

700
00:47:52,779 --> 00:47:54,017
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said;

701
00:47:54,319 --> 00:48:00,755
That Rasool Allah ﷺ put me ahead of many of his companions and took a lot of care of me.

702
00:48:00,828 --> 00:48:05,528
And we would see the manifestation of that in the rest of Seerah(سيرة).

703
00:48:06,194 --> 00:48:12,678
Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed an army of 3000 strong

704
00:48:13,345 --> 00:48:18,843
to attack the lands of the Romans in Ash-sham(ألشام).

705
00:48:20,598 --> 00:48:25,461
And this was to be the first encounter between the Muslims and the Romans

706
00:48:26,262 --> 00:48:29,359
and also the first encounter between Muslims and Christians.

707
00:48:29,988 --> 00:48:37,460
There was something unique this time in the appointment of the Umara'a(أمرآء), on this army, the leaders of this army,

708
00:48:38,092 --> 00:48:44,139
usually the cases that Rasool Allah ﷺ would appoint one Ameer(أمير) for the army and that's it.

709
00:48:44,839 --> 00:48:46,493
This time it was different,

710
00:48:46,866 --> 00:48:51,373
Rasool Allah ﷺ said that the Ameer(أمير) is Zaid Ibn Harissa(زيد بن حارثه)

711
00:48:51,744 --> 00:48:52,689
فَاِنْ اُصِيْبْ

712
00:48:52,957 --> 00:48:56,318
If he is killed, then Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر إبن أبي طالب)

713
00:48:56,525 --> 00:48:57,230
فَاِنْ اُصِيْبْ

714
00:48:57,254 --> 00:49:00,025
If he is killed, then Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة).

715
00:49:00,420 --> 00:49:08,038
So, Allah-O-Alam(الله اعلم) it could be that the risk and the danger of this encounter,

716
00:49:08,188 --> 00:49:17,081
demanded that Rasool Allah ﷺ take the additional step of appointing two Umara'a(أمرآء) as backup for the first

717
00:49:17,588 --> 00:49:21,218
or it could be because Rasool Allah ﷺ knew beforehand

718
00:49:21,964 --> 00:49:24,304
that they would be killed Allah-O-Alam(الله اعلم).

719
00:49:24,328 --> 00:49:28,141
But we don't find anywhere else in the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

720
00:49:28,165 --> 00:49:33,772
that Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed backup Umara'a(أمرآء), in case the first is killed.

721
00:49:34,455 --> 00:49:39,470
So this is something unique with what we refer to as Ghazwat Maota(غزوة المؤته).

722
00:49:39,565 --> 00:49:46,929
 There's something else that is unique with Ghazwat Maota(غزوة المؤته), this is the only time in Seerah(سيرة)

723
00:49:47,276 --> 00:49:52,226
where an army that is not led by Rasool Allah ﷺ is called Ghazwa(غزوة).

724
00:49:52,765 --> 00:49:56,741
Usually a Ghazwa(غزوة) is an army in which Rasool Allah ﷺ participates

725
00:49:57,098 --> 00:50:01,546
and a Sariyyah(سرية) is an army in which Rasool Allah ﷺ does not participate

726
00:50:01,799 --> 00:50:03,839
that is how it is in the books of Seerah(سيرة).

727
00:50:04,530 --> 00:50:07,449
So, whenever you see Ghazwa(غزوة) you know that Rasool Allah ﷺ was there

728
00:50:07,708 --> 00:50:12,255
and whenever you see the title Sariyyah(سرية), dispatch you know that Rasool Allah ﷺ was not there.

729
00:50:12,637 --> 00:50:16,254
With Maota(مؤته), it is called Ghazwa(غزوة) and all the books of Seerah(سيرة),

730
00:50:16,777 --> 00:50:20,494
I mean that's what Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري) calls it, that's what Ibn Hishaam(إبن هشام) calls it

731
00:50:20,518 --> 00:50:22,154
Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ), Al-Waqadie(ألواقدي)

732
00:50:22,408 --> 00:50:26,033
they all agree on calling this a as Ghazwa(غزوة) even though Rasool Allah ﷺ was not there.

733
00:50:26,057 --> 00:50:27,139
So, why, what's the reason?

734
00:50:27,179 --> 00:50:35,042
Some scholar said; Because of its huge importance, it was given this honorary title of being Ghazwa(غزوة)

735
00:50:35,483 --> 00:50:37,544
even though Rasool Allah ﷺ was not there.

736
00:50:37,986 --> 00:50:40,401
And this is the largest of Sarayah(سراية),

737
00:50:40,655 --> 00:50:44,610
because Sarayah(سراية) like we have seen in the past were small in number

738
00:50:44,650 --> 00:50:52,517
I mean a few hundred max, sometimes it would be as small as four or five would be a Sariyyah(سرية).

739
00:50:52,880 --> 00:50:54,311
But here we have 3000.

740
00:50:55,088 --> 00:50:56,605
There's a Hadith(حديث) in At-Tirimdhi(ألترمذي),

741
00:50:57,390 --> 00:50:58,954
however this Hadith(حديث) is Munqatah(منقطة),

742
00:50:58,994 --> 00:51:03,195
and Munqata(منقطة) is one of the types of weak Hadith(حديث).

743
00:51:04,082 --> 00:51:08,197
But there is another strong Hadith(حديث) that strengthens it,

744
00:51:08,237 --> 00:51:10,938
even though they're not the same in terms of the wording,

745
00:51:10,978 --> 00:51:15,055
but they are are talking, in principle about the same issue.

746
00:51:15,422 --> 00:51:18,043
This Hadith(حديث) in At-Tirimdhi(ألترمذي) states that

747
00:51:18,539 --> 00:51:23,757
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent out an army and among the members of this army

748
00:51:23,886 --> 00:51:28,261
would designate to go out with this army, was Abdullah Bin Rawaha رضي الله عنه

749
00:51:28,930 --> 00:51:31,223
and this army was to leave on Friday

750
00:51:31,460 --> 00:51:35,274
and Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) he mentions this Hadith(حديث) as evidence that

751
00:51:35,575 --> 00:51:40,148
the Muslims left out Madina in Ghazwat Maota(غزوة المؤته) on a Friday.

752
00:51:40,713 --> 00:51:44,820
Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) thought about it, he said well I'm one single person

753
00:51:44,845 --> 00:51:48,230
so if I stay because this army was supposed to leave at Fajr(فجر),

754
00:51:48,331 --> 00:51:52,427
 if I stay and pray Jumah(جمعه) with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

755
00:51:52,614 --> 00:51:55,914
I will be able to catch up with the army because I'm just one person

756
00:51:55,939 --> 00:51:57,833
because the army as a whole is slow

757
00:51:58,064 --> 00:52:01,782
but one individual can speed up and catch up with the rest.

758
00:52:02,079 --> 00:52:06,383
Rasool Allah ﷺ spotted him in Salah(صلاة),

759
00:52:06,407 --> 00:52:11,680
Rasool Allah ﷺ saw him and said: How come you stayed behind?

760
00:52:12,356 --> 00:52:15,559
Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) responded and said: O Messenger of Allah,

761
00:52:15,583 --> 00:52:16,852
اَرَدْتُّ اَنْ اُجَمِّعَ مَعَكْ

762
00:52:16,876 --> 00:52:18,729
I wanted to pray Jumu'ah(جمعه) with you.

763
00:52:19,475 --> 00:52:21,468
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

764
00:52:21,691 --> 00:52:27,201
لَوْ اَنْفَقْتَ مَا فِيْ الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا مَا اَدْرَكْتَ غَدْوَتَهُمْ

765
00:52:27,720 --> 00:52:36,951
If you spend all the money on earth you would not catch up with them these few hours

766
00:52:37,067 --> 00:52:41,041
where Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) stayed behind between Fajr(فجر) and Jumu'ah(جمعه).

767
00:52:41,294 --> 00:52:45,714
Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling him, if you spend all the money in the world,

768
00:52:45,905 --> 00:52:49,009
you will not catch up with him in terms of reward.

769
00:52:49,786 --> 00:52:52,304
We're not talking about if he stays behind completely.

770
00:52:52,511 --> 00:52:54,848
We're talking about if he catches up with them.

771
00:52:55,453 --> 00:52:57,302
Those few hours that he missed,

772
00:52:57,509 --> 00:53:01,661
he will never be able to make them up even if he spent all the money in the world.

773
00:53:02,315 --> 00:53:06,234
The authentic Hadith(حديث) which I was talking about that witnesses for this Hadith(حديث),

774
00:53:06,423 --> 00:53:08,255
is the saying of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

775
00:53:08,493 --> 00:53:12,699
لَغَدْوَةٌ اَوْ رَوْحَةْ فِيْ سَبِيْلِ الله خَيْرٌ مِنَّ الدُّنْيَا وَمَا فِيْهَا

776
00:53:12,985 --> 00:53:20,498
Leaving early with an army or coming back with them is better than the Earth and everything in it.

777
00:53:20,846 --> 00:53:22,959
Now, let's think about this for a moment,

778
00:53:22,983 --> 00:53:24,922
why did Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) stayed behind

779
00:53:24,947 --> 00:53:26,922
he didn't want to stay behind because of fear.

780
00:53:26,947 --> 00:53:29,885
He didn't want to leave Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

781
00:53:29,923 --> 00:53:31,051
That wasn't the case.

782
00:53:31,183 --> 00:53:34,989
He had the right intentions for staying behind the wanted to seek knowledge

783
00:53:35,300 --> 00:53:38,252
and seek knowledge from who not from a Shaikh(شيخ) or a great scholar,

784
00:53:38,292 --> 00:53:41,930
he wanted to seek knowledge from Rasool Allah ﷺ himself.

785
00:53:41,984 --> 00:53:44,773
He wanted to stay behind to receive the Ajr(أجر) of Jumu'ah(جمعه)

786
00:53:44,797 --> 00:53:47,400
and Jumu'ah(جمعه) with who with Muhammadﷺ.

787
00:53:47,424 --> 00:53:51,279
Nevertheless, Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling him that what you did is wrong.

788
00:53:51,854 --> 00:53:55,158
Those few hours that you missed, nothing can make them up for you.

789
00:53:55,795 --> 00:53:58,547
So Rasool Allah ﷺ was teaching the Sahabah(صحابه) a lesson

790
00:53:58,824 --> 00:54:02,121
that you are not excused from staying behind.

791
00:54:02,555 --> 00:54:05,710
We know that fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) can be with yourself.

792
00:54:05,847 --> 00:54:10,431
It can be with your wealth, or it can be with your tongue, because Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

793
00:54:10,455 --> 00:54:14,803
جَاهِدُوا الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ بِاَنْفُسِكُمْ وَ اَمْوَالِكُمْ وَاَلْسِنَتِكُمْ

794
00:54:14,986 --> 00:54:20,308
Fight the disbelievers with yourself and your wealth, and your tongues.

795
00:54:20,804 --> 00:54:26,046
However, fighting the Mushrikeen(مشركين) with ones, tongue alone is not enough.

796
00:54:26,269 --> 00:54:31,959
Otherwise, it would have been sufficient for the great scholars among the Sahabah(صحابه),

797
00:54:32,134 --> 00:54:36,324
to sit behind in Madina and not go out with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

798
00:54:36,555 --> 00:54:41,616
but we know that the scholars of the Sahabah(صحابه) like, Obaye Ibn Ka'ab(أبي إبن كعب) and Muadh Bin Jabal(معاذ إبن جبل)

799
00:54:42,191 --> 00:54:45,959
and the poet of the Sahabah(صحابه) Hassaan Ibn Thabit(حسان بن ثابت),

800
00:54:46,057 --> 00:54:48,152
they all went out in the Ghazawaat(غزوات),

801
00:54:48,224 --> 00:54:51,262
and their knowledge was not an excuse for them to stay behind.

802
00:54:51,800 --> 00:55:00,804
In fact, Rasool Allah ﷺ himself, whom the Ummah(امة) depends on for learning the revelation, he did not stay behind, and he said,

803
00:55:01,085 --> 00:55:05,186
that I wish that I can join with every army that leaves.

804
00:55:05,706 --> 00:55:11,271
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان), and Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن بن عوف), who used to finance the armies,

805
00:55:11,700 --> 00:55:18,510
 this support by their wealth was not sufficient, for them, they had to go out themselves.

806
00:55:18,808 --> 00:55:23,204
And no one tried to justify and make sense of this by saying that,

807
00:55:23,365 --> 00:55:25,461
well, if they go out they would be killed.

808
00:55:25,501 --> 00:55:28,639
Therefore it's better for them to stay behind and just support with their wealth.

809
00:55:28,679 --> 00:55:30,946
No they had to go out themselves.

810
00:55:31,315 --> 00:55:34,132
And here Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة)

811
00:55:34,156 --> 00:55:36,932
that no matter what you do, you will not catch up with them.

812
00:55:36,956 --> 00:55:38,678
Even though you prayed Jumu'ah(جمعه) with me,

813
00:55:38,829 --> 00:55:42,566
even though you stayed behind with the intention of learning, Talab-Ul-Ilm(طلب العلم),

814
00:55:42,654 --> 00:55:45,164
that's not an excuse, you should have went out.

815
00:55:45,691 --> 00:55:49,606
The army reached to As-sham(ألشام) to Jordan, present the Jordan.

816
00:55:49,813 --> 00:55:58,157
And they received intelligence that the Romans have heard, of their marching

817
00:55:58,848 --> 00:56:00,659
 and they have mobilized an army.

818
00:56:00,739 --> 00:56:03,801
Now, the news that they received wasn't really that good.

819
00:56:04,616 --> 00:56:09,073
If they receive news that the army that, they are meeting

820
00:56:09,515 --> 00:56:13,755
would be an army of 3000 like them, that would have been fine.

821
00:56:14,290 --> 00:56:19,469
If they received intelligence that the Army's twice their numbers 6000 that would be fine.

822
00:56:20,051 --> 00:56:22,973
In fact, we might speculate if they received the news

823
00:56:22,997 --> 00:56:26,448
the army is 10 times their number, such as 30,000.

824
00:56:26,678 --> 00:56:28,194
They would be fine with that.

825
00:56:28,914 --> 00:56:31,022
These are the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

826
00:56:31,354 --> 00:56:34,401
courage and bravery and Eeman(إيمان) and Tawakkul(توكل) on Allah.

827
00:56:34,991 --> 00:56:41,982
But the news was that they are facing an army of 200,000 strong,

828
00:56:42,212 --> 00:56:46,934
100,000 Roman soldiers, professional Roman soldiers,

829
00:56:46,958 --> 00:56:54,109
in addition to 100,000 Christian Arabs, these are the allies of the Romans in the land of As-sham(ألشام).

830
00:56:54,850 --> 00:56:56,464
This is disastrous news.

831
00:56:56,726 --> 00:56:59,134
3000 facing 200,000.

832
00:56:59,158 --> 00:57:03,471
I mean, so far the Muslims have never ever heard of such numbers.

833
00:57:04,304 --> 00:57:08,059
In the past, the largest force that they would face,

834
00:57:08,415 --> 00:57:11,438
for example, in the Battle of Al-Khandaq(ألخندق) was 10,000.

835
00:57:12,207 --> 00:57:16,360
Here they're facing an army of 200,000.

836
00:57:16,638 --> 00:57:18,923
And then, who are we talking about?

837
00:57:18,947 --> 00:57:21,923
We're talking about the soldiers of the Roman Empire.

838
00:57:22,208 --> 00:57:24,034
I mean, they had a reputation.

839
00:57:24,413 --> 00:57:34,217
The Romans and the Persians had the reputation of having strong fighting forces, well trained, well armed, professional soldiers.

840
00:57:34,600 --> 00:57:39,299
We're not talking about tribesmen, we're talking about the professional army.

841
00:57:39,740 --> 00:57:41,849
So, this issue demanded the Shura'a(شورى).

842
00:57:41,889 --> 00:57:47,203
So the Ameer(أمير) Zaid Ibn Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) consulted with the prominent Sahabah(صحابه).

843
00:57:47,368 --> 00:57:48,391
What should we do?

844
00:57:48,729 --> 00:57:52,583
Some of them said let's send messenger to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

845
00:57:52,623 --> 00:57:54,935
and ask him what should be done well, let's, let's wait.

846
00:57:55,708 --> 00:57:57,984
Abdullah Bin Rawaha رضي الله عنه said;

847
00:57:58,207 --> 00:58:04,449
Men, what you dislike is what you have come forth to seek, martyrdom.

848
00:58:05,685 --> 00:58:11,442
Listen to this, Men, what do you dislike is what you have come forth to seek.

849
00:58:12,048 --> 00:58:16,380
Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) is reminding them with their original intentions,

850
00:58:16,626 --> 00:58:20,965
you are companions of Rasool Ullah, you came out with the intention.

851
00:58:21,110 --> 00:58:25,678
Every one of you every single one of you wants to die Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

852
00:58:25,917 --> 00:58:29,088
that's our ultimate goal, ultimate desire.

853
00:58:29,444 --> 00:58:33,374
If that is what we want, how come now we are disliking it.

854
00:58:34,206 --> 00:58:36,981
I mean, what is the reason, you're asking us to pause and wait?

855
00:58:37,157 --> 00:58:40,881
What is the reason you're asking us to not face the enemy?

856
00:58:41,541 --> 00:58:43,071
Is it fear of death?

857
00:58:43,417 --> 00:58:47,914
Well, what's the point in that we all came here with the intention of dying Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

858
00:58:48,282 --> 00:58:49,452
So, he reminded them.

859
00:58:49,476 --> 00:58:52,038
وَذَكِّرْ فَاِنَّ الذِّكْرَىٰ تَنْفَعُ الْمُؤمِنِيْنْ

860
00:58:52,181 --> 00:58:55,792
Remind them because the reminder will benefit the believers,

861
00:58:55,999 --> 00:58:57,752
Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) then told them.

862
00:58:57,889 --> 00:59:02,272
We are not fighting by means of our numbers or strength,

863
00:59:02,487 --> 00:59:09,080
we are combating them only with this religion, with which Allah has honored us.

864
00:59:09,159 --> 00:59:15,645
Go forth, it will only result in one of the two good outcomes, either victory or martyrdom.

865
00:59:15,669 --> 00:59:17,984
اِحْدَ الْحُسْنَيَيْنْ اِمَّاالنَّصْرُ وَاِمَّا الشَّهَادَةْ

866
00:59:18,071 --> 00:59:24,455
This is what every Muslim looks up to, either to to win against the enemy in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) or die Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

867
00:59:25,246 --> 00:59:29,784
That encouraged them and they said: By Allah, Ibn Rawaha(إبن رواحة) is right.

868
00:59:30,749 --> 00:59:34,330
And they decided to go forth, no matter what the consequences are.

869
00:59:34,801 --> 00:59:38,918
And this tells us about the spirit of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

870
00:59:38,942 --> 00:59:42,130
Their thoughts, their concern was with Aakhira(آخرة).

871
00:59:42,821 --> 00:59:45,842
That's what they were concerned about! Aakhira(آخرة) and not Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

872
00:59:45,866 --> 00:59:52,595
And we are facing Allahعَزّوجَلّ, let's go on the other side of this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) will be meeting Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

873
00:59:53,462 --> 00:59:59,029
وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

